<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Illyria</h1><p class="st-meta">1816 CE – 1849 CE · capital Laibach</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Austrian crown land formed from the former French Illyrian Provinces, uniting Slovene and Adriatic lands under one title for three decades.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/illyrian-provinces">Illyrian Provinces</a>, it kept the name and in 1816 created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/illyrian-kingdom">Kingdom of Illyria</a> as a crown land of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>. It comprised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-gorizia">Gorizia and Gradisca</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/histria">Istria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a>, and for a few years Civil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>, which returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1822.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was mainly an administrative label: it was divided into two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">governorates</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ljubljana">Laibach</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a>, each run by Austrian officials under the system of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klemens-von-metternich">Metternich</a>, with provincial estates of little power. Laibach hosted the congress of 1821 on revolutions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Slovene cultural life grew, with the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france-preseren">France Prešeren</a> writing in Laibach in the 1830s and 1840s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the revolutions of 1848, the 1849 constitution dissolved the kingdom into separate crown lands: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-littoral">Austrian Littoral</a>. The emperor kept the title King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyria">Illyria</a> until 1918.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-illyria.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Illyria" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Illyria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1816 CE – 1849 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Laibach</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Francis I, Ferdinand I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Slovene, German, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Königreich Illyrien</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1832&amp;focus=kingdom-of-illyria" aria-label="Kingdom of Illyria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5023 556 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Illyria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5343 812L5343 812M5343 812L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5343 812h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5343 812h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5343 812h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1832&amp;focus=kingdom-of-illyria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
